  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0098' consists of five tables: User, Technical_solution, Employee, Technical_solution_feedback, and Technical_solution_evaluation.\nThe User table is used to store user information, including email, gender, name, phone number, and a unique user ID. Each row in this table represents a user. The User_ID is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity as it uniquely identifies each user.\nThe Technical_solution table stores information about technical solutions, including the expected end date of implementation, start date of implementation, solution description, solution name, and status. The Technical_solution_ID is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity for each solution.\nThe Employee table stores information about employees, including contact number, email, gender, and name. The Employee_ID is the primary key, ensuring entity integrity for each employee.\nThe Technical_solution_feedback table is used to store feedback about technical solutions. It includes feedback content, feedback date, satisfaction level, and suggestions from users. The User_ID and Technical_solution_ID are foreign keys referencing the User and Technical_solution tables respectively, ensuring referential integrity.\nFinally, the Technical_solution_evaluation table stores evaluations of technical solutions. It includes evaluation content, date of evaluation, evaluation indicators, evaluation results, and the Technical_solution_ID and Employee_ID are foreign keys referencing the Technical_solution and Employee tables respectively, ensuring referential integrity.\nThis schema is exhaustive and covers all the necessary aspects of the data it will hold, from domain integrity (each column has the appropriate data type and allows null values or not) to referential integrity (foreign keys reference the primary keys of the related tables).",
  "gold_question": "In modern enterprises, the management and evaluation of technology solutions is an important part of ensuring that technology investment generates maximum value and promotes business innovation. With the rapid development of information technology, various technology solutions (such as software tools, hardware equipment, cloud services, artificial intelligence systems, etc.) have become key means for enterprises to improve efficiency, reduce costs, and optimize products and services. However, how to effectively manage and evaluate these technology solutions to ensure that they meet business needs and achieve expected results has become a challenge for enterprises.\nTherefore, enterprises need a dedicated technology solution management and evaluation system. Management of technology solutions: record and track the selection, implementation and maintenance process of various technology solutions to ensure that they can continue to meet the technology needs of the enterprise.\nEvaluation of solutions: evaluate the effectiveness of various technology solutions, evaluate their cost-effectiveness, implementation progress, user feedback, etc.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0098.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0098\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Technical_solution` (\n  `Technical_solution_ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `solution_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `solution_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Technical_solution_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Employee` (\n  `Employee_ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Employee_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Technical_solution_feedback` (\n  `Feedback_ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Technical_solution_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `feedback_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `feedback_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `satisfaction_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `suggestions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Feedback_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_feedback_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_feedback_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Technical_solution_ID`) REFERENCES `Technical_solution` (`Technical_solution_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Technical_solution_evaluation` (\n  `Evaluation_ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `Technical_solution_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Employee_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `evaluation_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `evaluation_indicators` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `evaluation_results` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Evaluation_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Technical_solution_ID`) REFERENCES `Technical_solution` (`Technical_solution_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `technical_solution_evaluation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Employee_ID`) REFERENCES `Employee` (`Employee_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
